# Shell scripts run on Linux: keep LF even in a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true),
# or bash on the VM fails with "$'\r': command not found".
*.sh text eol=lf
# Env templates and Compose/workflow files are read on Linux too; a stray \r would end up inside a value.
*.example text eol=lf
*.versions text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
# The monitoring stack's configuration, read on the VM (Runbook 7): the Alertmanager template is rendered line by line.
*.alloy text eol=lf
*.template text eol=lf
monitoring/AI_SOURCE text eol=lf
